  "$comment": "Journey-wall manifest (RESTRUCTURE-2026-07-30 §5/§7). Board (x,y) on screen pages is DERIVED from this file by 73-screens-from-states.js — walls are a generated output, never a hand arrangement, so regeneration reproduces them (FR-008). Wall kinds: 'flow' = steps left-to-right in journey order; 'hub' = hub board first column, spokes to its right. states[board] stack BELOW that board (dark twins, empty/error/locked states). Steps may name boards that do not exist yet (S/send/sign, receipts) — 73 skips absent boards but reserves their column, so adding the board later lands it in place. Boards on a page but in no wall fall into an auto 'misc' band after the last wall (legacy grid).",
